    "result_text": "The full suite is green. `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper, so `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class \u2014 it passes, and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` derivation for owner creation, following the codebase's existing conventions for derived owner fields (like `membershipNumber`, `locality`, `checkDigit`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added optional `birthDate` (ISO `date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema.\n   - Added read-only `ageBand` (string) to the `Owner` response schema, documented as `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`, null when no birth date.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`**\n   - Added the persistent `birthDate` field (`birth_date DATE` column) with getter/setter.\n   - Added a `@Transient getAgeBand()` that computes whole years from `birthDate` to `registrationDate` (`Period.between`) and bands them: `<18 \u2192 MINOR`, `18\u201364 \u2192 ADULT`, `\u226565 \u2192 SENIOR`; returns null when either date is absent. Measuring against `registrationDate` (per the spec) keeps the band stable over time.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres/schema.sql`)\n   - Added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. The hsqldb schema is the one the tests load (`ddl-auto=none`); the others were updated for consistency.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` wires `birthDate` (request\u2192entity) and both `birthDate`/`ageBand` (entity\u2192response) automatically by property name \u2014 no mapper changes needed, matching how the other derived fields already work.\n\nNo git operations were performed (this directory isn't a git repository, and you didn't ask for a commit).",
