    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the codebase's established pattern precisely. `Owner` already hosts a family of `@Transient` derived-string getters computed from the entity's own fields \u2014 `getLocality()`, `getIdentityKey()`, and especially `getContactPreference()` (`model/Owner.java:244-278`). The new `getAgeBand()` is the same shape: a self-contained derivation over the owner's own `birthDate`/`registrationDate`, null-guarded, placed directly after its siblings. A maintainer would find this the natural home.\n\n- The `birthDate` field, getter, and setter sit with the other persisted fields/accessors in the conventional order; nothing is duplicated.\n- Banding logic is genuinely additive \u2014 it doesn't bloat an existing method or reach outside the entity, and measuring against `registrationDate` keeps it a pure function of the owner's own state, consistent with the \"derived from the owner's own fields\" comment style used by the neighbors.\n- Schema changes are mirrored across all four dialects, and the OpenAPI additions (`birthDate` writable, `ageBand` `readOnly`) match how the derived values are modeled.\n\nNo structural concerns.",
